WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.170
Speaking of women in sports,

2
00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:05.030
Thursday is baseball's Opening Day,

3
00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:08.108
and boy, have we got the perfect guest here to celebrate,

4
00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.710
Tiki!
(Tiki chuckles)

5
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:12.610
She is a former pro baseball player,

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:16.160
who played in the All-American Girls Baseball League,

7
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.937
the real life league that inspired the phenomenal film,

8
00:00:19.937 --> 00:00:21.340
"A League of Their Own."

9
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.700
Please welcome an ace pitcher from Southern California,

10
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.127
Maybelle Blair!
(audience applaud)

11
00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:29.377
(whooping)

12
00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.620
How are you?
Hey Maybelle, how are you?

13
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.297
Oh God, the old girl couldn't be better, Tiki.

14
00:00:36.297 --> 00:00:37.970
(chuckles) Oh, I love it, I love it!

15
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.270
All right, Maybelle, tomorrow is opening day,

16
00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.130
who are you going to be watching?

17
00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:44.070
Oh my God!

18
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.195
Every ball game I can watch,

19
00:00:46.195 --> 00:00:49.360 line:15%
with my Dodgers, and my Angels, my Red Sox,

20
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.940 line:15%
and now with the Florida Marlins (indistinct),

21
00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.430 line:15%
but, it can mean-
Yes

22
00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.660 line:15%
Be the first woman general manager, can you believe that?

23
00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.580
That shows the advancement

24
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.280
of women in professional sports.

25
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.350
We're seeing professional football teams

26
00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.180
have women coaches, right?
Yep!

27
00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.560
So we know that it's changing slowly but surely.

28
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.072
It started because of you,

29
00:01:10.072 --> 00:01:11.016
Maybelle!
That's right!

30
00:01:11.016 --> 00:01:13.346
(audience cheering)
Yeah, can you believe that?

31
00:01:13.346 --> 00:01:16.390
This old 94-year-old girl helped a little bit,

32
00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:17.760
not much.
(Tiki chuckles)

33
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.050
But, oh my God!

34
00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.783
I'm so excited with what's happening.

35
00:01:20.783 --> 00:01:23.560
Maybelle, I have a question for you, which is,

36
00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.560
you're young, it's in the 1940s,

37
00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.350
obviously there's a very different time for women.

38
00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.440
What is a good tip for young people today

39
00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:38.290
to hook into their passion?
The main thing today

40
00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.310
is to get out there and do your damnedest,

41
00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.460 line:15%
because it is going to happen Drew.

42
00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:46.890 line:15%
We are going to open it up, we're going to do our...

43
00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.370 line:15%
We're going to get a new league,

44
00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:50.910 line:15%
in fact, we're working on it now.

45
00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.480 line:15%
We're trying to get our own museum going,

46
00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:57.380 line:15%
and it's happening, and if you love it follow it.

47
00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.330 line:15%
'Cause look at Tiki, he's sitting there,

48
00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:00.260 line:15%
he probably didn't think

49
00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.870 line:15%
he was gonna play professional football, but he did,

50
00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:06.598
and look what he did, and us girls can do the same thing.

51
00:02:06.598 --> 00:02:08.506
(applause)
And we're so excited to-

52
00:02:08.506 --> 00:02:11.006
(indistinct chatter)
(audience claps)

53
00:02:11.006 --> 00:02:12.170
That is so true Maybelle.

54
00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:13.003
I have four daughters,

55
00:02:13.003 --> 00:02:15.940
I don't want them to be limited by anything, so absolutely!

56
00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.700
You're an inspiration Maybelle,

57
00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.730
thank you so much for being you.

58
00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:22.630
I mean, seriously, you started something profound,

59
00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:25.080
and we're still feeling it.
Yeah, absolutely!

60
00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:25.913
Well, thank God!

61
00:02:25.913 --> 00:02:29.000
I am so thrilled about it, it has opened up college sports

62
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:29.870
and everything,

63
00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.170
now in the WNBA,

64
00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:35.450
and I'm so proud of those girls, they're doing their thing,

65
00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.870
and girls are getting scholarships,

66
00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.690
and baseball is finally opening their eyes

67
00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:42.960
that we can play baseball.

68
00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.330
So, let us have an opportunity to play,

69
00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.520
let these girls have that, that's what I'm working for

70
00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.263
while I'm on this side of the grass.

71
00:02:50.263 --> 00:02:52.320
(chuckles)
Well, and all the data

72
00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.210
in the world says that young girls

73
00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:57.140
who get involved in sports,

74
00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:01.203 line:15%
just have a better shot at like, quality focus,

75
00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.620 line:15%
lovely friendships.

76
00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.528 line:15%
It's just-
Educational opportunities,

77
00:03:05.528 --> 00:03:06.361 line:15%
scholarships,

78
00:03:06.361 --> 00:03:07.257 line:15%
all those things
Yes!

79
00:03:07.257 --> 00:03:08.231
You're absolutely right, Drew.

80
00:03:08.231 --> 00:03:12.350
Thank you Maybelle for showing, especially in the 1940s,

81
00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:13.820
what was possible.

82
00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.820
And please go to our show website,

83
00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.420 line:15%
and find out how you can support women in baseball,

84
00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.891 line:15%
and Maybelle's Museum.

85
00:03:20.891 --> 00:03:22.856 line:15%
(audience cheering)
Oh my gosh, yeah!

86
00:03:22.856 --> 00:03:25.360
And I (indistinct)
(applause)

87
00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:28.340
And you were a Peoria Redwing, in fact, Maybelle,

88
00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:31.800
we have a clock here dedicated to Peoria, Illinois,

89
00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.960
and our affiliate station, WMBD.

90
00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.720
Oh, how wonderful!
Well-

91
00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.888
You can't beat that.
You can't!

92
00:03:38.888 --> 00:03:40.350
And you can't beat you Maybelle,

93
00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:42.589
thank you so much for coming on the show today.

94
00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:45.506 line:15%
